Dependency provenance
Rust packages and exact sources/checksums are pinned in Cargo.lock; npm packages
and integrity hashes are pinned in package-lock.json. Dependencies remain
separate upstream packages, not relicensed source files in this repository.
The main pipeline dependencies are:
- Stylo 0.22.0, https://github.com/servo/stylo, MPL-2.0.
  Kept exclusively as a dependency; no MPL source is copied or adapted.
- Taffy 0.15.1, https://github.com/DioxusLabs/taffy, MIT.
- Parley 0.12.0, https://github.com/linebender/parley, Apache-2.0 OR MIT.
- html5ever 0.40.1, https://github.com/servo/html5ever, MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- AnyRender 0.14.0 and anyrender_vello_cpu 0.18.0,
  https://github.com/DioxusLabs/anyrender, MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- Vello CPU 0.3.0, https://github.com/linebender/vello, Apache-2.0 OR MIT.
- Peniko 0.6.1, https://github.com/linebender/peniko, Apache-2.0 OR MIT.
- data-url 0.3.2, https://github.com/servo/rust-url, MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- png 0.18.1, https://github.com/image-rs/image-png, MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- Serde 1.0.229 and serde_json 1.0.154, https://github.com/serde-rs,
  MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- Clap 4.6.7, https://github.com/clap-rs/clap, MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- Playwright 1.58.2, https://github.com/microsoft/playwright, Apache-2.0.
- pngjs 7.0.0, https://github.com/pngjs/pngjs, MIT.

Chromium is downloaded by Playwright as an external reference tool. It is not
embedded in or redistributed by our native renderer. Its bundled notices remain
in the external browser installation.

third-party/rust-dependencies.json records every resolved Rust package's origin,
exact version, licence expression and upstream commit where included in the
published crate. Git dependencies use their pinned source URL. The lockfile
checksums identify registry packages even when upstream omitted VCS metadata.
Regenerate with python tools/dependency-notices.py after dependency updates.

All fixture markup, CSS, SVG paths and comparison tools are original work for
html-native-renderer under Apache-2.0, apart from the embedded font noted above.
